Is the implication $\mathrm{P}
e\mathrm{NP}\Longrightarrow(\mathrm{NP},\mathrm{PSamp})
subseteq\mathrm{AvgP}$ true? That is, assuming \(\mathrm{P}
e \mathrm{NP}\), must there exist a language \(\mathrm{L}\in \mathrm{NP}\) and a polynomial-time samplable distribution ensemble \(D=\{D_{n}\}\) such that no deterministic exact decider for L runs in average polynomial time under D, in the moment-based sense defined below?
